    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d908">

                <pb facs="0995" n="903" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg903"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8900</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Persia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-20T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegrams February 18, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d908-f1"/> and 9 p.m.,
                    surprising in view of your recent report that there was no important news in
                    Persia. The Department must have an immediate and complete report on Turkish and
                    German propaganda in Persia. By what means is it being carried on, what success
                    is it making, and how can it be guarded against? Is present Persian Government
                    pro-Ally, pro-German, or truly neutral in its sympathies? Is Persia seeking the
                    withdrawal of English troops from Persia in good faith or for the purpose of
                    aiding Germany and Turkey as soon as this is done? What does Persia really want
                    and expect America to do? Investigate these matters very discreetly, but also
                    very thoroughly, and reply.</p>
                <p>The situation in Persia may become a matter of vital importance. It is essential
                    that you realize its importance and keep the Department fully informed of actual
                    situation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
